  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**B**.You are a junior analyst at a linguistic research firm. Your first task is to build a simple tool to perform a basic analysis on a given text string. This tool will help senior researchers quickly get primary metadata about text samples.\n\nYou need to write a program that takes a single string as input and performs three specific operations:\n\n\nConvert the entire string to its uppercase equivalent.\nCount the total number of vowels (A, E, I, O, U) in the uppercase string.\nDetermine if the uppercase version of the string is a palindrome. A string is a palindrome if it reads the same forwards and backward.\n\nInput Format\nA single line containing the string `S`.\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nThe output should consist of three lines:\n\n\n\nThe first line should contain the uppercase version of the input string.\nThe second line should contain the count of vowels.\nThe third line should contain either \"Palindrome\" or \"Not a Palindrome\".",
